# FCCZ4_GR — NRPy-generated fCCZ4 module for Dendro-GR

GENERATED FILE - DO NOT EDIT.
Generator: nrpy.infrastructures.Dendro
Regenerate with: `python -m nrpy.examples.dendro_fccz4 ...`
Module ABI: `$MODULE_ABI_HASH`

## What this module contains

- `generated/` — every file is rendered from the frozen NRPy snapshot
  (gridfunction registry, CodeParameter registry, CFunction registry):
  state header, parameter struct, per-CFunction sources, CMake source list,
  and semantic-hash constants.
- `include/`, `src/` — the mock-vehicle runtime context (`fccz4Ctx`) and the
  entry point `fccz4Solver`.
- `pars/` — the generated TOML profile(s).
- `tests/` — generated project self-tests (state registry, parameter
  registry, padding, memory offsets, upwind selection, RHS, initial data,
  exact-name selection, algebraic projection, constraint diagnostics).

No formulation content is authored in this module: the names, order,
stencils, and expressions come from the NRPy registries, and the Dendro
runtime owns only lifecycle, mesh, and execution (whitepaper sections
4.1/9.16).

## Deferred (recorded, not dropped)

- This module refuses to configure inside a Dendro-GR tree that defines a real
  `dendro5` target: its generated sources are compiled against the mock host
  types, so linking them to the real host would be a silent type mismatch
  (section 13.2).  Remove it with `tools/remove_generated_module.py`.
- The real Dendro-GR host integration (CRTP context, `ot::DVector`/`ts::Ctx`
  lifecycle, remesh, checkpoint, VTU) lands after the pinned Dendrolib
  capability gates (section 13.2; see `dendrolib_pin.json` /
  `dendrolib_capabilities.json` in the NRPy Dendro infrastructure).  This
  module builds against the mock host stubs in `dendro_mock.hpp`.
- Physical boundaries (PR 10) and the checkpoint ABI (PR 11) are separate
  qualified profiles; `manifest/boundaries.json` in the parent project is an
  explicit deferral record.  Projection, initial-data conversion and
  diagnostics are registered in this profile, and their manifests describe
  the registered CFunctions rather than a deferral.